Root cause:
The bug was caused by the incorrect handling of the data size when copying from user space in the `bpf_test_init` function. Instead of using the size specified by the user (`kattr->test.data_size_in`), the code mistakenly attempted to copy the maximum data size, which could lead to buffer overflows and sporadic failures with the error code EFAULT. The fix involved ensuring that only the user-specified size was copied, preventing potential memory access violations.
